Are you passionate about translating cutting-edge science into meaningful outcomes for patients? Join a collaborative, high-performing medical communications team where your scientific expertise directly informs impactful programs for leading pharmaceutical and biotech clients. In this role, you’ll partner across disciplines to shape strategy, elevate scientific storytelling, and contribute to a culture built on excellence, innovation, and long-standing client success. This is an opportunity to grow within a dynamic organization known for its award-winning work, strong client partnerships, and commitment to professional development.

Position Summary &nbsp;

The Scientific Director leads the strategic direction and execution of scientific content across client engagements, ensuring all deliverables are evidence-based, scientifically rigorous, and aligned with broader brand and business objectives. As the scientific lead, the Scientific Director sets the vision for content strategy and drives integration of scientific, clinical, and market insights to deliver high-impact programs. The Scientific Director partners closely with cross-functional team leads to shape programs, guide decision-making, and elevate the role of scientific leadership within the account. This role includes oversight of multiple projects and teams, mentorship of junior and mid-level staff, and accountability for quality, consistency, and strategic alignment across all deliverables. &nbsp;

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

Content Development &nbsp;

• Set the strategic direction for scientific content across accounts, ensuring alignment with client&nbsp; objectives , brand strategy, and medical priorities. &nbsp;

• Provide senior-level oversight and final accountability for the quality, accuracy, and consistency of all deliverables. &nbsp;

• Maintain oversight of content development processes and training. &nbsp;

• Guide teams in interpreting complex clinical data and translating insights into differentiated scientific communications. &nbsp;

• Identify &nbsp;opportunities to elevate content through strategic storytelling and market insights. &nbsp;

• Maintain deep therapeutic area&nbsp; expertise . &nbsp;

Collaboration &amp; Communication &nbsp;

• Serve as a senior scientific partner to clients. &nbsp;

• Provide strategic recommendations and solutions. &nbsp;

• Lead or oversee scientific discussions with clients and key opinion leaders. &nbsp;

• Direct cross-functional teams toward strong execution. &nbsp;

• Build collaborative stakeholder relationships. &nbsp;

• Contribute to proposal and pitch development. &nbsp;

Account Support &nbsp;

• Oversee large accounts or groups of smaller accounts. &nbsp;

• Review timelines, budgets, and resource requirements. &nbsp;

• Drive operational consistency and best practices. &nbsp;

• Ensure regulatory and compliance standards are met. &nbsp;

• Identify &nbsp;and mitigate risks proactively. &nbsp;

• Support resource planning and account health. &nbsp;

• Apply financial understanding including&nbsp; utilization , burn, and scope management. &nbsp;

Scientific Leadership &amp; Team Development &nbsp;

• Lead and inspire scientific teams. &nbsp;

• Establish standards of excellence. &nbsp;

• Support team engagement and change initiatives. &nbsp;

• Address team dynamics and provide direct feedback. &nbsp;

• Contribute to department standards, processes, and training. &nbsp;

• Identify &nbsp;capability gaps and partner with leadership on solutions. &nbsp;

Team Integration &amp; Professional Skills &nbsp;

• Demonstrate leadership presence and sound judgment. &nbsp;

• Manage multiple priorities effectively. &nbsp;

• Delegate while&nbsp; maintaining &nbsp;accountability. &nbsp;

• Promote collaboration and continuous improvement. &nbsp;

• Communicate confidently with senior stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Adapt to evolving client and business needs. &nbsp;

Additional Responsibilities for People Managers&nbsp; &

Who we are&nbsp;

At Twilio, we’re shaping the future of communications, all from the comfort of our homes. We deliver innovative solutions to &nbsp;hundreds of thousands of businesses&nbsp; and empower millions of developers worldwide to craft personalized customer experiences.

Our dedication to remote-first work , and strong culture of connection and global inclusion means that no matter your location, you’re part of a vibrant team with diverse experiences making a global impact each day. As we continue to revolutionize how the world interacts, we’re acquiring new skills and experiences that make work feel truly rewarding. Your career at Twilio is in your hands.
.

Hiring and how we work

We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&nbsp;

Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&nbsp;
